## What YOU Must Implement

### ❌ Pass 2: Link Detection - Same Technology (Empty Skeletons Provided)

Three methods in `{{TECHNAME}}_module.py` are provided as **empty skeletons**:

1. **`full_parse()`** - Detect function/method calls in source code
2. **`resolve()`** - Match call names to actual target objects  
3. **`save_links()`** - Create links using CAST SDK

**Without implementing these methods, your extension will:**
- ✅ Create all objects correctly
- ❌ Create ZERO links between {{LANGUAGE}} objects
- ❌ Show no call relationships within {{LANGUAGE}} code

**See the "Implementing Link Detection (Pass 2)" section below for guidance.**

### ❌ Application Level: Cross-Technology Links (Empty Template Provided)

One method in `{{TECHNAME}}_application_level.py` is provided as an **empty template**:

1. **`end_application()`** - Create links between {{LANGUAGE}} and other technologies

**Without implementing this method, your extension will:**
- ✅ Create all {{LANGUAGE}} objects correctly
- ✅ Create links within {{LANGUAGE}} (if Pass 2 is implemented)
- ❌ Create ZERO links to Java, SQL, or other technology objects
- ❌ Show no cross-technology relationships in CAST Imaging

**See the "Implementing Cross-Technology Links (Application Level)" section below for guidance.**

